ROLE: systems_reviewer  VOTE: yellow
PROMPT_VERSION: v001
EXISTING_IMPLEMENTATIONS: [
  {system: "SGLang / RadixAttention", url: "https://www.lmsys.org/blog/2024-01-17-sglang/", overlap: "Automatic KV-cache reuse via prefix matching across LLM calls; overlaps on avoiding repeated in-context computation, but not on skipping an external RAG lookup because answer content is already resident in the live window."},
  {system: "vLLM Automatic Prefix Caching", url: "https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/design/prefix_caching.html", overlap: "Hashes prompt-token blocks and reuses computed KV blocks for matching prefixes; token-prefix cache, not semantic/context-span retrieval gating."},
  {system: "TensorRT-LLM KV cache reuse", url: "https://nvidia.github.io/TensorRT-LLM/advanced/kv-cache-reuse.html", overlap: "Shares KV pages for requests starting with the same prompt to reduce TTFT; no evidence of pre-retrieval in-context-presence checks."},
  {system: "LMCache", url: "https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache", overlap: "Shares long-context/prefix KV across vLLM instances and lowers repeated long-context TTFT; no evidence of RAG retrieval-call suppression based on live-window content."},
  {system: "Self-RAG / FLARE / Adaptive-RAG", url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.11511 ; https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.06983 ; https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.14403", overlap: "Adaptive retrieval decides when/how much to retrieve based on reflection tokens, low-confidence future generation, or query complexity; closest published overlap, but not specifically an in-context-residency gate with independent item-id GT."}
]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: mechanism
SCALE_REALISM: Synthetic L0 only. The anti-circular GT/check split is clean, and matched-random control is the right systems baseline for the proposed gate. But realistic workload validity is unproven: no real long-horizon agent/RAG traces, no real embedding, no real retrieval latency/token accounting, and no model-in-the-loop task recovery after wrong skips.
RATIONALE: No shipping OSS system found that directly implements “skip retrieval because the needed content is already in the current live context window.” Existing systems already solve adjacent redundancy at the inference layer via token-prefix/KV reuse: SGLang explicitly retains KV for prompts and generation results in a radix tree for prefix search/reuse/eviction, while vLLM and TensorRT-LLM reuse hashed/paged KV blocks for same-prefix requests. That makes this not an inference-systems cache insight; it is a RAG-layer retrieval-suppression mechanism plus measurement protocol. The packet’s evidence supports the mechanism on a constructed generator: redundant fraction 0.235-0.816, lexical AUC 0.835-1.000, and matched-random accuracy delta CI > 0 with tau=0.3 skipping 39% at modeled accuracy 1.000. However, because the workload, redundancy labels, and task-success model are generated, the systems claim does not yet hold at realistic scale/workload. L1 must use real agent+RAG logs with in-context-presence labels, production-like retrieval costs, a real sentence embedding/check, and end-to-end model accuracy.
